---
/**
 * /adult-drivers-ed/texas/expired-out-of-state-license — the two-year line.
 *
 * Rebuilt 2026-10-13 on the hook → answer → loop → funnel recipe. DPS waives the exams and driver education for an
 * out-of-state license that is valid or not expired over two years (law.dpsWaiverText). Past that line the reader
 * is a new applicant, and at 18 through 24 the course applies, so the page ends in the course band.
 */
import AdeGuide from '../../../components/ade/AdeGuide.astro';
import { law, fees, itd, newResident } from '../../../data/ade-eligibility';

const base = '/adult-drivers-ed/texas';
const url = `${base}/expired-out-of-state-license`;

// The one-breath answer: meta description and the first sentences of the lede.
const answer = `An out-of-state license not expired over two years still transfers to Texas without the knowledge or driving test, per DPS. Past two years both apply, and at ${law.requiredBand} so does the six-hour course.`;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'My out-of-state license expired. Do I need Texas drivers ed?', a: `Not if it expired two years ago or less. DPS waives the knowledge and skills exams and the adult driver education requirement for someone 18 or older holding a valid out-of-state license "or license not expired over two years". Past two years, the waiver no longer applies, and if you are ${law.requiredBand} the six-hour course comes back.` },
  { q: 'How is the two-year window measured?', a: 'From the expiry date printed on the license, not from the last time you drove. Find the card before you assume either way, because people routinely misremember expiry dates by a year.' },
  { q: 'Can I drive in Texas on an expired out-of-state license after I move?', a: `Not under the grace period. DPS lets new residents drive for up to ${newResident.graceDays} days on a valid, unexpired license from another U.S. state, U.S. territory, Canadian province or qualifying country. An expired card is outside that rule; within two years it still counts as the basis for the transfer.` },
  { q: 'What if I cannot find my old license?', a: 'Contact the issuing state for a driving record or a replacement. DPS needs to see the license to accept it as the basis for a transfer, and surrendering it is part of the process.' },
  { q: 'What if it expired more than two years ago?', a: `Then you are treated as a new applicant: the knowledge test, the driving skills test, the ${itd.adultName} video, and the six-hour adult driver education course if you are ${law.requiredBand}. At 25 or older the course is not required.` },
];

const next = [
  { href: `${base}/new-resident-out-of-state-license`, title: 'If the license is still valid', blurb: 'The straight transfer: what you surrender, what you register, and the 90-day window.' },
  { href: `${base}/do-i-need-adult-drivers-ed`, title: 'Do you need the course?', blurb: 'The Texas rule by age and by the license you already hold.' },
  { href: `${base}/how-to-get-a-texas-license-as-an-adult`, title: 'Starting over, step by step', blurb: 'The full new-applicant process, from the course to the card, in order.' },
  { href: `${base}/cost`, title: 'What the course costs', blurb: 'The price, and what it includes.' },
];
---

<AdeGuide
  title="Expired Out-of-State License in Texas: The Two-Year Line for Drivers Ed and Tests | Road Ready Safety"
  description={answer}
  url={url}
  eyebrow="Eligibility"
  h1="Expired out-of-state license? Under two years it still transfers to Texas. Past two, you start over"
  lede={`${answer} The line is measured from a date most people get wrong, and which side of it you are on, by age, is below.`}
  faqs={faqs}
  dateModified="2026-10-13"
  updated="October 13, 2026"
  band={{ eyebrow: 'Expired more than two years', heading: 'Past the two-year line at 18 to 24? The course applies again, and the exam is in it' }}
  next={next}
  sources={[
    { label: 'Texas DPS, Moving to Texas: A Guide to Driver Licenses and IDs', href: 'https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/moving-texas' },
    { label: 'Tex. Transp. Code §521.1601, Driver Education Required; Exception', href: 'https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/TN/htm/TN.521.htm' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">Where is the two-year line for an expired out-of-state license?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Two years past the expiry date, per DPS. The statute exempts anyone holding &ldquo;a valid driver&rsquo;s
      license issued by another state&rdquo;, and DPS is more specific in practice, and more generous:
    </p>
    <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-border pl-5 py-1 m-0">
      <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px] italic m-0">&ldquo;{law.dpsWaiverText}&rdquo;</p>
      <cite class="text-sm text-text-muted not-italic">&mdash; Texas DPS, Moving to Texas</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      The clause that matters is <strong>&ldquo;or license not expired over two years.&rdquo;</strong> Inside
      two years, an expired card still gets the transfer treatment: no knowledge test, no skills test, no
      driver education. Outside it, none of that carries over.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">Do you need drivers ed if it expired more than two years ago?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Only if you are {law.requiredBand}; the knowledge and skills tests apply at any age.
    </p>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 m-0 list-disc marker:text-text-subtle">
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>Expired within two years, any adult age.</strong> Treated as a transfer. Surrender the card, pay the ${fees.newLicense18to84} fee, take the vision test.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>Expired more than two years ago, and you are {law.requiredBand}.</strong> New applicant. Six-hour adult driver education course, knowledge test, skills test, {itd.adultName} video.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>Expired more than two years ago, and you are 25 or older.</strong> New applicant, but no driver education requirement. The tests and the video still apply.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">How do you know which side of the line you are on?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Measure from the expiry date printed on the card, not from the last time you drove. Find the license
      before you plan around either answer. If you cannot find it, the issuing state can give you a driving
      record or a replacement, and DPS needs to see the license to accept it as the basis for a transfer.
    </p>
  </section>
</AdeGuide>
